// TYPECHECK THE RESEARCH PROBES.
//
// `tsconfig.json` covers `src`, `tests`, `scripts` and nothing else, so the
// forty-odd `.mts` harnesses under `../research/` — every one of which imports
// signatures straight out of `game/src` — were checked by nothing at all. A
// rename in `src` broke them silently and the breakage only surfaced the next
// time somebody happened to run that probe, in a project whose entire evidence
// base IS those probes.
//
// Extends the shipped config so the probes are held to exactly the same rules
// the game is: `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`,
// `verbatimModuleSyntax`. Two are relaxed, and only two:
//
//   noUnusedLocals / noUnusedParameters — a probe legitimately decodes more
//   than it prints on any given run, and an unused intermediate is how a
//   measurement gets parked while the next one is written. Refusing those would
//   make the check a nuisance rather than a rail, and neither can mask a drift
//   in a signature, which is what this config exists to catch.
//
// `../research` is NOT in this git repository (it is the operator's local
// working tree), so this config is deliberately NOT part of `npm run build`:
// a clean checkout has nothing to point it at. `npm run typecheck:research`
// runs it and says out loud when the tree is absent — see
// `scripts/typecheck-research.mjs`.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false
  },
  "include": ["../research/**/*.mts"],
  // TWO ARCHIVED DIRECTORIES, AND THE EXCLUSION IS BY DIRECTORY SO THAT A NEW
  // PROBE ANYWHERE ELSE UNDER research/ IS PICKED UP WITHOUT ANYONE DECIDING TO.
  //
  // Both hold drivers that were WRITTEN IN AND RUN FROM `game/scripts/` and
  // moved here afterwards, which their own headers say:
  // `view/fixround/INDEX.txt` — "the drivers in drivers\ ran from game\scripts\
  // via npx vite-node scripts/_verify-fidelity.mts ... (moved here afterwards to
  // leave the repo tree as the fix round left it)"; and
  // `view/fixround/drivers/_verify-tables.mts` — "Temporary; deleted after the
  // round." Their `../src/...` and `../tests/...` specifiers therefore resolve
  // from `game/scripts/` and from nowhere else, and `./_verify5.mts` is a
  // sibling import that only a bundler run accepts.
  //
  // MEASURED, so the exclusion is a number and not a hand-wave: including them
  // contributes 102 of the 127 errors the very first run found — 67 TS2307
  // "cannot find module ../src/...", 12 TS5097 ".mts extension" and 23 TS7006
  // implicit-any parameters that only exist because the modules those callbacks
  // come from could not be resolved. Every one is a statement about where the
  // file is sitting, not about the code. They are artefacts of finished rounds;
  // nothing runs them again. The remaining 25 are real drift in 10 live probes.
  "exclude": ["../research/view/round5/verify/harness", "../research/view/fixround/drivers"]
}
